# 🚖 Uber Trip Analysis – Power BI Dashboard (Overview Analysis)

An interactive Power BI dashboard that analyses **103,728 Uber trips (June 2024, New York area)** to understand booking trends, revenue, trip efficiency, payment behaviour, vehicle performance and location demand.

> Scope: Dashboard 1 – **Overview Analysis**.

---

## 📌 Business Objective
> Full requirement document: [`docs/Problem_Statement.md`](docs/Problem_Statement.md)

Analyse Uber trip data to gain insights into booking trends, revenue and trip efficiency so that stakeholders can make data-driven decisions on pricing, driver availability and customer experience.

## 🗂️ Dataset
| File | Rows | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `Uber_Trip_Details.xlsx` | 103,728 | Trip ID, Pickup/Drop-off time, passenger count, trip distance, pickup & drop-off location IDs, fare amount, surge fee, vehicle type, payment type |
| `Location_Table.xlsx` | 265 | LocationID, Location (zone name), City (borough) |

**Period covered:** 1 June 2024 – 30 June 2024

## 🧱 Data Model
- `Trip Details` (fact) → `Location Table` (dimension) on **PULocationID** (active relationship – pickup)
- `Trip Details` → `Location Table` on **DOLocationID** (inactive relationship – activated with `USERELATIONSHIP` for drop-off analysis)
- `Calendar Table` for date slicing
- Disconnected table `Dynamic Measure` as a **measure selector** (Total Bookings / Total Booking Value / Total Trip Distance)

## 📊 KPIs
| KPI | Value |
|---|---|
| Total Bookings | **103.7K** |
| Total Booking Value (fare + surge) | **$1.55M** |
| Average Booking Value | **$15.0** |
| Total Trip Distance | **349K miles** |
| Average Trip Distance | **3.4 miles** |
| Average Trip Time | **16 min** |

## 🧩 Dashboard Components
1. **Measure selector** – switches the donut charts between Total Bookings / Total Trip Distance / Total Booking Amount, with dynamic titles
2. **By Payment Type** – donut chart
3. **By Trip Type (Day / Night)** – donut chart
4. **Vehicle Type Analysis** – table with bookings, booking value, average booking value and trip distance
5. **Total Booking Amount by Day** – area chart for daily trend
6. **Location Analysis** – most frequent pickup, most frequent drop-off, farthest trip
7. **Top 5 Locations by Bookings**
8. **Most Preferred Vehicle by Pickup Location**
9. **Slicers** – Date and City

## 🔍 Key Insights
**Overall**
- 103,728 trips generated about **$1.55M** revenue; of this ≈ **$1.35M is base fare** and ≈ **$205K (13%) is surge fee**. Surge was applied on **~64% of trips**.
- Typical trip is short: **median 2.3 miles**, average 3.4 miles, **median duration ~10.7 min**. 79% of trips have a single passenger.

**Vehicle types**
- **UberX is the clear leader: 38,744 trips (37%) and $584K revenue (38%)** – more than double any other vehicle.
- Average booking value is almost the same for every vehicle (**$14.9 – $15.1**), so premium categories (Black, Comfort, XL) are not earning a premium per trip → a **pricing optimisation opportunity**.

**Payment**
- **Uber Pay 67%**, **Cash 32%**, Amazon Pay / Google Pay < 1% combined.
- Uber Pay trips have a higher average value (~$15.8) than Cash trips (~$13.3).

**Time patterns**
- **~80% of trips are day trips** (6 AM – 7 PM), ~20% are night trips.
- Demand builds from 6 AM, stays high between **12 PM and 6 PM (peak ≈ 3 PM, ~7.9K trips)** and is lowest at **3–4 AM (~330 trips/hour)**.
- Daily bookings range from ~1.9K to ~4.9K. Highest days: **26 June (4,947)** and **25 June (4,744)**; lowest: **14 June (1,934)** and **7 June (2,099)** – both Fridays.
- Average trips per day by weekday: Wed ≈ 3.9K, Sun ≈ 3.8K, Tue ≈ 3.8K, Sat ≈ 3.7K, Mon ≈ 3.7K, Thu ≈ 2.8K, **Fri ≈ 2.3K (weakest)**.

**Locations**
- **Manhattan accounts for ~92% of all pickups** (and ~86% of drop-offs), Queens ~5%, Brooklyn ~1% – the service is overwhelmingly a Manhattan business.
- Most frequent pickup: **Penn Station / Madison Sq West (4,475)**, followed closely by **Upper East Side North (4,459)** and Upper East Side South (4,124).
- Most frequent drop-off: **Upper East Side North (4,024)**.
- Upper East Side / Lenox Hill zones dominate both pickups and drop-offs → keep driver supply concentrated there.
- UberX is the most preferred vehicle at every top pickup location.
- Farthest trip: **144.1 miles** from **Lower East Side → Crown Heights North**, ~532 min, $563.79 (UberX, 28 June 2024). Only 52 trips are longer than 30 miles – these are outliers.

## 💡 Recommendations
- Increase driver availability around Penn Station, Upper East Side and Lenox Hill during 12 PM – 6 PM.
- Review pricing of Uber Black / Comfort / XL since their average booking value is equal to UberX.
- Investigate why Fridays (especially 7 & 14 June) show much lower demand – data gap, weather, event or supply issue.
- Promote digital payments (Uber Pay) as they bring higher average ticket values.
- Use surge more selectively; it already touches ~64% of trips.

## ⚠️ Data Quality Notes & Fixes
- **City column in `Location_Table` was wrong for ~90 zones** (e.g. Lower East Side, Midtown East, Park Slope, East Village were tagged with the wrong borough; `Bronx` and `The Bronx` were split). This made the City slicer and any city-wise numbers unreliable. A corrected file is provided: `data/Location_Table_Cleaned.xlsx` (every change is listed in its *Change Log* sheet).
- ~0.9% of trips (926) have an *Unknown* pickup zone (LocationID 264/265).
- A few trips have extreme durations (up to ~24 hours) and 2 trips have zero/negative duration – these inflate the **average trip time (16 min)** versus the **median (~10.7 min)**. Excluding trips longer than 3 hours (and zero/negative ones) gives an average trip time of ~13 min.
- 3 location names are duplicated across IDs (*Corona*, *Governor's Island/Ellis Island/Liberty Island*) – they refer to the same place.

